      "id": "p0023-b001",
      "kind": "caption",
      "source": {
        "text": "There are several ways of handling cultural matters in translation. In academia, it's standard practice to translate everything literally and include lots of explanatory footnotes. In entertainment, it's more common to localize foreign cultural references by replacing them with something similar, but more familiar to the target audience",
        "raw": "There are several ways of\nhandling cultural matters\nin translation. In academia,\nit's standard practice\nto translate everything\nliterally and include lots\nof explanatory footnotes.\nIn entertainment, it's\nmore common to localize\nforeign cultural references\nby replacing them with\nsomething similar, but\nmore familiar to the\ntarget audience",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
